cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Jakarta ISPU Classification: Comparing Ensemble and Deep Learning Models with SHAP Interpretation"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Eriel Setiawan"
    family-names: "Dewantoro"
    affiliation: "Universitas Bina Sarana Informatika"
repository-code: "https://github.com/erielsdewantoro/jakarta-ispu-classification"
abstract: >-
  Binary classification of daily Jakarta Air Pollution Standard Index (ISPU) categories
  for 2020-2024, comparing Random Forest and XGBoost against LSTM and GRU under a
  chronological train-test split, with SHAP-based interpretation of the selected ensemble
  model. The repository documents a structural target-leakage property of the dataset and
  an asymmetry in input representation between the two model families, both of which
  constrain how the reported metrics should be read.
keywords:
  - air quality
  - ISPU
  - Jakarta
  - binary classification
  - random forest
  - xgboost
  - LSTM
  - GRU
  - SHAP
  - explainable AI
  - target leakage
license: MIT
